    {
      "id": "fi-001",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:20:00Z",
      "user": "cto_zhang",
      "text": "@liwei Security alert escalated to this group. All technical documents and decision memos you produce should include a dedicated '## Rationale' section explaining WHY the chosen approach was selected. This is required for audit trail."
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-002",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:22:00Z",
      "user": "liwei",
      "text": "Understood. All technical documents will include a ## Rationale section."
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-003",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:25:00Z",
      "user": "devops_wang",
      "text": "The AWS key in the leak has AKIA prefix. That means it's a long-term IAM user credential. We need to disable the key in IAM, not just block it at network level."
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-004",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:27:00Z",
      "user": "liwei",
      "text": "Confirmed. AKIA = long-term IAM key. Containment method = disable_iam_user_key. If it were ASIA (STS temp), we'd need a deny-all policy with DateLessThan condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-005",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:30:00Z",
      "user": "cto_zhang",
      "text": "What's the industry context for how quickly similar incidents are remediated?"
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-006",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T08:32:00Z",
      "user": "liwei",
      "text": "Per GitGuardian State of Secrets Sprawl 2024: only 2.6% of leaked secrets are revoked within 1 hour of notification. Over 90% remain active 5 days post-detection. We need to move fast."
    },
    {
      "id": "fi-007",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-10T09:40:00Z",
      "user": "liwei",
      "text": "CloudTrail log analysis in progress."
